d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x},{f}_{1}(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-2.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)=2,{f}_{2}(x)={e}^{x},{f}_{1}(x)=0,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340678 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340679 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340680 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340681 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340682 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1041 "selection" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340678 13194139535265 true] [17592186340677 1110 #uuid "25ab82cd-1aa9-517a-9c8e-e69c0b654c96" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340678 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340678 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535265 true] [17592186340678 1111 #uuid "8a98b0d4-db57-58c0-8523-402735c11fb8" 13194139535265 true]