\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & =a[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{1}]+b[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-x(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =ax\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+bx\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-ax{y}_{1}-bx{y}_{2} \\\\  & =a[x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x{y}_{1}]+b[x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is **not** linear.\nTo see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})(a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\na{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2})=a{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.\\,\\times \n$$" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340706 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340707 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340708 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340709 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340710 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1041 "selection" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340710 13194139535265 true] [17592186340705 1110 #uuid "f76c28be-4b0a-546d-9193-263aead3144e" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340706 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535265 true] [17592186340706 1111 #uuid "a9ca37dd-f675-58c0-a7cb-25a4ed8d99c9" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340707 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535265 true] [17592186340707 1111 #uuid "846ac46d-8fff-5f8c-b26a-5aa8df04b65a" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340708 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535265 true] [17592186340708 1111 #uuid "e6a0e51d-63f2-5ad9-8ead-d55efbeb09e9" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340709 1034 "III only" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535265 true] [17592186340709 1111 #uuid "90df5ac0-4c38-59aa-8d77-2a24d53e2b8e" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340710 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535265 true] [17592186340710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535265 true] [17592186340710 1111 #uuid "811e4d5a-0614-5de5-b253-faf0eecf3eb8" 13194139535265 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-130076" 17592186340580 "q-130076/selection" 17592186340581 "q-130076/selection/4fb17f261e904acf135ebcd64b2c6ee5d6d28610997d2d0c2fbe0ff4712d8f99" 17592186340582 "q-130076/selection/